{#
  The three steps, lifted verbatim from the home page so the two can never
  drift. Numbered because this genuinely is a sequence — step 2 cannot happen
  before step 1.

  `processHeading` overrides the default, so the service pages can ask the
  question the reader has just formed instead of repeating the home heading.
#}
<section class="sec" id="process">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal" style="margin-bottom: clamp(48px, 6vw, 68px);">
      <h2>{{ processHeading | default("How a project runs.") }}</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step reveal" style="--d:0">
        <span class="step-n">
          <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-message"/></svg>
          01
        </span>
        <h3>Tell me what you need</h3>
        <p>We talk through your business, your customers and what the site has to do. I ask the questions that decide the rest of the build.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="step reveal" style="--d:1">
        <span class="step-n">
          <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-grid"/></svg>
          02
        </span>
        <h3>I design and build it</h3>
        <p>You see the site as it comes together, not just at the end. Revisions are part of the price, not an upsell.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="step reveal" style="--d:2">
        <span class="step-n">
          <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-rocket"/></svg>
          03
        </span>
        <h3>We go live</h3>
        <p>I handle the domain, the hosting and the launch. Then I stay reachable for the updates that come after.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
